thread:
maria: FYI — support case from Acme. They upgraded some infra and now their app using @redwood/node v3.0.1 gets 404 when calling models.list. Request id rwd-12345. Repro attached.
evansupport: @evan can you take a look?
evan: Can you paste the minimal repro and the exact error? Did they change API host or auth?
maria: Repro:
```js
// package.json: "@redwood/node": "3.0.1"
const Redwood = require('@redwood/node');
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_KEY });
async function list() {
  const res = await client.models.list();
  console.log(res);
}
list().catch(e => console.error(e));
```
Error shown: 
```
Error: Request failed with status 404
GET https://api.redwood.ai/v2/models -> 404 Not Found
{"error":"endpoint_not_found","message":"No route for /v2/models"}
```
evan: hmm :thinking: v3.0.1 should still call /v1/models on the server we run in prod. This looks like a publish mismatch where the package JS references the new v2 routes but the API hasn't rolled out v2. Can you share the npm tarball sha and dist-tags?
maria: npm info for customer: @redwood/node@3.0.1, dist-tags: latest -> 3.0.1. Tarball sha256: abcdef1234567890... Customer installed via npm yesterday.
raj: I pulled the publish logs — looks like the publish job started before the build finished on the release runner. The types and package.json bumped to v3 (v2 routes) but the compiled bundle is from an older artifact path. Race condition in our CI. :facepalm:
ci-bot: publish pipeline run #9123 completed. Release created: @redwood/node@3.0.1 (artifact: 3.0.1.tgz)
evan: Ok. Short-term options: ask customer to pin back to @redwood/node@3.0.0 (works), or we can hotfix and republish 3.0.2. Alternative temporary workaround is to call the HTTP endpoint directly (manual path) until we republish:
```js
const fetch = require('node-fetch');
await fetch('https://api.redwood.ai/v2/models', {
  headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.REDWOOD_KEY}` }
});
```
maria: Customer prefers npm fix. Can we fast-track 3.0.2 patch and republish?
evan: I'll open a GH issue and a PR to re-run the build and republish as 3.0.2 with correct artifacts. Also adding a smoke test to the publish pipeline to assert the runtime paths match package metadata. ETA: today EOD. @raj can you own the pipeline change?
raj: Yep, will add a smoke test that installs the built tarball in a clean node container and verifies a simple client call doesn't 404. I'll also rollback the dist-tag to 3.0.0 for now. Done.
maria: Noted — informed customer to pin to 3.0.0. They reported app is working with the pin. Will re-open if they hit anything else. Thanks everyone :thumbsup:
evan: Filed internal ticket rwd-sdk-176 to track the hotfix and pipeline fix. Assigning to SDK eng.
